# 2026-07-29 — HOSTNAME CANONICALISATION CANNOT BE DONE IN THIS FILE. Tested and confirmed:
# Cloudflare Pages matches _redirects rules on the PATH ONLY, so absolute-URL sources like
#   https://www.thaiear.com/*  https://thaiear.com/:splat  301
# deploy successfully and then silently never match. Don't re-add them.
# The problem they were meant to solve is real: www.thaiear.com serves a full 200 copy of
# every page and Search Console indexed it separately from the apex, splitting ranking
# signal (12 of the homepage's 42 impressions landed on www). Both hosts emit a canonical
# pointing at the apex, but a canonical is a hint, not a directive.
# The fix lives at ZONE level instead: Cloudflare dashboard → thaiear.com → Rules →
# Redirect Rules → "www to apex", If hostname equals www.thaiear.com → dynamic 301 to
# concat("https://thaiear.com", http.request.uri.path), preserve query string.
# thaiear.pages.dev is NOT in the zone so no rule can reach it; it relies on its canonical
# tag, which is acceptable because nothing links to it.
